    <string name="guide_content"><![CDATA[
<b>1. Starting &amp; Stopping Editor</b><br>
<small>Main Interface GodMode Pro → Master switch ON</small><br>
<br>&#8226; <b>Notification</b> — Tap to toggle Start / Exit Editor<br>
&#8226; <b>Quick Settings Tile</b> — One-tap toggle (alternative when notifs disabled)<br>
&#8226; Disabling master switch exits edit mode and removes the notification<br><br>

<b>2. Tool Panel</b><br>
<small>A semi-transparent panel appears on the right when editing</small><br>
<br>&#8226; <b>Slider</b> &ensp;&ensp;&ensp;&ensp;&ensp; Select elements by hierarchy depth<br>
&#8226; <b>Toggle Position</b> &ensp; Panel left / right side<br>
&#8226; <b>Feed Mode</b> &ensp;&ensp;&ensp; Toggle ON / OFF (default OFF)<br>
&#8226; <b>Remove·Modify</b> &ensp; Expand respective menus<br>
&#8226; <b>Prev·Next</b> &ensp;&ensp;&ensp; Navigate elements one by one<br>
<br><b>Volume Keys</b><br>
&#8226; <b>Single Press</b> &ensp; Navigate prev/next when panel is open<br>
&#8226; <b>Double Press</b> &ensp; Quick double-tap → toggle panel open / close<br>
&#8226; <b>Long Press</b> &ensp;&ensp; Rapid continuous element switching<br>
<br>Red overlay = selected element&ensp;│&ensp;Orange overlay = inside a list (RecyclerView)<br><br>

<b>3. Selecting Elements</b><br>
<br>&#8226; <b>Tap</b> &ensp;&ensp;&ensp;&ensp; Touch any element directly<br>
&#8226; <b>Slider</b> &ensp;&ensp; Drag the vertical bar on the panel<br>
&#8226; <b>Buttons</b> &ensp; Tap Prev / Next arrows on the panel<br>
&#8226; <b>Volume Keys</b> Press Vol Up/Down when panel is open<br><br>

<b>4. Feed Mode</b><br>
<br>&#8226; <b>OFF</b> (default) — Each operation affects only the single selected element<br>
&#8226; <b>ON</b> &ensp;&ensp;&ensp; — Changes to list items apply to all structurally identical items<br><br>

<b>5. Remove Mode</b><br>
<br><b>Preview</b> — Temporarily hide the element, tap again to restore<br>
<br><b>Block</b> — Select an element, then tap <b>Block</b> on the toolbar<br>
<br><i>Rules and screenshots saved automatically</i><br><br>

<b>6. Modify Mode</b><br>
① Select element → tap <b>Modify</b> button to open property panel<br>
② Adjust properties:<br>
&ensp;&#8226; <b>Width·Height</b> &ensp; Slider or manual input (0–2000)<br>
&ensp;&#8226; <b>Alpha</b> &ensp;&ensp;&ensp;&ensp;&ensp; 0–255 slider<br>
&ensp;&#8226; <b>Position</b> &ensp;&ensp; Arrow keys, 10px per step<br>
&ensp;&#8226; <b>Text</b> &ensp;&ensp;&ensp;&ensp;&ensp; Edit TextView content<br>
&ensp;&#8226; <b>Image</b> &ensp;&ensp;&ensp; Pick from gallery for ImageView<br>
③ Tap <b>Preview</b> on the toolbar to hide or restore the property panel<br>
④ Tap <b>Save</b> in the property panel to persist this target, or <b>Cancel</b> to revert<br><br>

<b>7. Rule Management</b><br>
<br><b>View &amp; Details</b><br>
&#8226; Tap a package name to enter rule list; menu filters: All / Remove / Modify<br>
&#8226; Tap a rule → swipe to browse screenshots, view info, depth<br>
&#8226; Set custom alias and toggle visibility in details<br>
<br><b>Delete</b><br>
&#8226; Details page menu → delete single rule<br>
&#8226; Filter first in list → delete only that category<br>
&#8226; &quot;All&quot; view → delete all rules (with confirmation)<br>
&#8226; <b>Long-press</b> a package in settings → clear all its rules at once<br>
<br><b>Backup &amp; Restore</b><br>
&#8226; Details page menu → backup single rule<br>
&#8226; Filtered list backup → exports current category only<br>
&#8226; &quot;All&quot; view export → all rules<br>
&#8226; Settings menu → select .zip backup file to restore<br>
<br><i>Backups include screenshots and images; rules take effect immediately after restore</i><br><br>

<b>8. Notes</b><br>
<br>&#8226; Only works in <b>third-party apps</b> activated in LSPosed<br>
&#8226; Launcher, system UI, keyboard, headless apps, and GodMode Pro itself are <b>not editable</b><br>
&#8226; After a crash, a dialog appears on next launch with a copyable log<br>
&#8226; Quick Settings tile works even when notifications are disabled
    ]]></string>

